# Observability — {{.ProjectTitle}}

## Logging

{{.ProjectTitle}} standardizes strictly on **`github.com/phuslu/log`** for high-performance structured logging. It delivers the fastest execution speeds in the Go logging ecosystem with zero heap allocations in critical paths.

### Benchmark Comparison

| Logger | Time (ns/op) | Memory (B/op) | Allocations (allocs/op) |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: |
| **`github.com/phuslu/log`** | **~48 ns/op** | **0 B/op** | **0 allocs/op** |
| `rs/zerolog` | ~150 ns/op | ~0 B/op | 0 allocs/op |
| `uber-go/zap` | ~140 ns/op | ~120 B/op | 1 allocs/op |
| `log/slog` (Go stdlib) | ~190 ns/op | ~16 B/op | 1 allocs/op |
| `sirupsen/logrus` (deprecated) | ~1,200 ns/op | ~1,400 B/op | ~24 allocs/op |

### Usage Example

```go
import "github.com/phuslu/log"

log.Info().
    Str("trace_id", traceID).
    Str("span_id", spanID).
    Str("method", req.Method).
    Str("path", req.URL.Path).
    Int("status", res.Status).
    Msg("trace")
```

**Logging Security Rules (Never Log):**
- Plaintext passwords, pins, private keys
- Full Authorization / Bearer tokens
- Cardholder PANs, CVV, or payment provider credentials
- Sensitive customer PII

Field masking is automatically handled in `internal/middleware/trace.go`.

