## OpenTelemetry & SigNoz Integration

### Architecture

```
[HTTP Request]
       │
  Trace Middleware ──> [OpenTelemetry Tracer] ──> OTLP gRPC (localhost:4317)
       │
  phuslu/log (Log Entry)
       │
  OtelLogWriter Bridge ──> [OpenTelemetry Logger] ──> OTLP gRPC (localhost:4317)
                                                              │
                                                      [SigNoz Collector]
                                                              │
                                                       [SigNoz Web UI]
                                                    (http://localhost:3301)
```

Each log record includes `trace_id` and `span_id`. When clicking a trace in SigNoz, all correlated log lines appear directly under the trace timeline.

### Database Tracing (GORM)

Database query spans are captured using `gorm.io/plugin/opentelemetry/tracing` configured with production security & debugging options:

```go
db.Use(tracing.NewPlugin(
    tracing.WithoutQueryVariables(), // Parameterized placeholders ($1, ?) to prevent secret leakage
    tracing.WithoutMetrics(),        // Omit DBStats metrics reporting overhead
    tracing.WithoutServerAddress(),  // Omit internal DB IP/host from span attributes
    tracing.WithRecordStackTrace(),  // Record full Go call stack trace on query errors
))
```

### Outbound HTTP Client Tracing

All external third-party HTTP calls wrapped with OpenTelemetry client tracing:

```go
// Option A: Via Circuit Breaker (Recommended for all 3rd-party calls)
client := resty.NewWithClient(circuitbreaker.NewClient())

// Option B: Direct HTTP client wrap
client := resty.NewWithClient(telemetry.WrapClient(nil))
```

### Starting SigNoz on Local Docker / OrbStack

Run the provided Makefile targets:

```bash
# 1. Start SigNoz + OpenTelemetry Collector (auto-initializes via official SigNoz Foundry CLI)
make signoz-start

# 2. Open SigNoz UI in your browser
open http://localhost:3301

# 3. Stop SigNoz containers
make signoz-stop

# 4. Clean up SigNoz containers and volumes
make signoz-clean
```

### Configuration

Set in `config.yml`:
```yaml
opentelemetry:
  host_grpc: "localhost:4317"
```

Or via environment variable in `.env`:
```bash
OTEL_HOST_GRPC=localhost:4317
```

If `host_grpc` is left empty, the application runs standalone with console logging only.

